plugins/bp303 - notices for the BP303 package (bp303.bass, bp303.a64.rmp)

BP303's voice is BLACKPYRAMIDS_303's, the TB-303 voice of the OT Kyoti FW project (a track machine for the Octatrack
MKI), ported to floating point C for the Sidecar. BLACKPYRAMIDS_303 began as a port of Robin Schmidt's Open303 and was
recalibrated on the TB-303's circuit and against recordings of a real one; its reference/BLACKPYRAMIDS_303.md says
which part is whose.
  Taken from:  https://github.com/Zac-Kyoti/octatrack-kyoti-fw  commit 109f54c
               reference/BLACKPYRAMIDS_303.md      the voice and every value
               tools/ot303/twin.h                  the engine (the integer twin of the DSP code), step for step
               tools/ot303/cf/params.c, record.c   the knobs to the engine's words, the eases, the accent sweep
               tools/ot303/cf/body_tables.h, params_const.h, halfband2x.h, body/gen_body.py   the tables and constants
               tools/ot303/body/bp_cf.cpp          the reference renderer (the note rules; the comparison in README.md)
  Licence:     MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Zac Kyoti and the OT Kyoti FW contributors (LICENSE.kyoti, that project's
               LICENSE unchanged)
  Built on:    Open303, https://github.com/RobinSchmidt/Open303 (pinned by that project at 313bf0d9): the oscillator
               blend and square shaper, the TeeBee ladder and its fitted coefficient formulas, the envelopes, accent,
               slide, the post filters' structure, the knob-to-parameter formulas.
               MIT, Copyright (c) 2009 Robin Schmidt (LICENSE.open303, as that project carries it)
The DSP56300 assembly, the ColdFire runtime and the Octatrack parts of that project are not ported and not in this
package. bp303_tables.h holds six of its generated tables unchanged (the knob laws); bp303.c is a rewrite of the voice
in float (its header lists what is whose and what the Sidecar changes). No Elektron or Roland material is in either.
"BP303" names the machine after BLACKPYRAMIDS_303; it is not affiliated with or endorsed by any synthesizer maker.

The port and the glue (bp303.c, manifest.json, the Makefile, tests/): MIT, Copyright 2026 trigcondition and
contributors (LICENSE). The package links sdk/rmp/shim (MIT).
